$ enola gc --help
exit: 2
--- stdout
--- stderr
Usage: enola gc [flags] [repo_path|config_path]

Report what this repository's architecture history holds, and remove what it no
longer needs.

With no flags it removes only garbage — segment directories no revision refers
to. Thinning and pruning discard things a reader could still reach, so each
needs asking for.

Revisions whose contents are dropped keep their summary line: the timeline stays
complete, and only replay is lost. `log --backfill` can rebuild them.

Flags:
  -dry-run
    	report what would be removed and change nothing
  -prune-working
    	remove working revisions (snapshots of uncommitted trees) from the log entirely
  -thin-older-than string
    	drop the stored contents of revisions older than this (e.g. 90d, 720h); their summary lines stay
